  "worked_solution": "The logarithms share the same base, and so we can combine them using the quotient rule, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2) & =1 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}) & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the equation for $x$ using the usual methods.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x/2)} & ={e}^{1} \\\\ \\frac{x}{2} & =e \\\\ x & =2e\\end{aligned}\n$$",
